\ul Procedure:\ulnone      Use a very hydraulic tensile testing machine and batty extensometer.\par
                        Take readings of load in half ton increments against extensometer.\par
                        Readings. At the yield point remove the extensometer (to prevent\par
                        Damage) and take further readings of load against extension using\par
                        Dividers set at    .increment. Continue until specimen fractures \par
\ul Graphs:\ulnone      1.     Plot load against extension for the complete experiment \par
                  2.    Plot load against extension up to the yield point only showing\par
                         this part of the graph to a more suitable scale.\par
\ul Calculations:\ulnone     calculate  Young modulus for mild steel\par
                                         Young stress\par
                                         Ultimate stress\par
                                         Fracture stress (using reduced area of cross-section)\par
                                          Percentage elongation over gauge length\par
                                          Percentage  reduction in area.\par
  \ul Preparation:\ulnone      Examine the testing machine and make brief notes in your notebook\par
                          about its basic principles of operation. Decide what readings you\par
                          Will need to take, draw up tables for results and prepare the paper.\par
\ul Contact a member of staff before proceeding further\par
